## 6. Extensibility — registering a third backend (FR-10)

A test stub backend lives in its own package. It has no edits in core (`internal/storage/*`) or `cmd/bd/*`.

```go
// File: internal/storage/teststub/store.go
//go:build test_stub

package teststub

import (
    "context"
    "github.com/steveyegge/beads/internal/storage"
)

func init() {
    storage.RegisterDriver(storage.BackendType("teststub"), openTestStub)
}

type Store struct { /* in-memory state */ }

var _ storage.Storage              = (*Store)(nil)
var _ storage.BulkIssueStore       = (*Store)(nil)
var _ storage.DependencyQueryStore = (*Store)(nil)
var _ storage.AnnotationStore      = (*Store)(nil)
// ... other MUST capabilities

func openTestStub(ctx context.Context, cfg storage.ConnectionConfig) (storage.Storage, error) {
    return &Store{ /* ... */ }, nil
}
```

The test binary blank-imports it:

```go
// cmd/bd/store_test_main.go
//go:build test_stub

import _ "github.com/steveyegge/beads/internal/storage/teststub"
```

The MUST-capability test (`TestMustCapabilitiesAreImplemented`, P1 §8) iterates over `storage.RegisteredBackends()` — the stub is checked automatically. **No core edits.** This is the FR-10 acceptance.

P2's PR does NOT ship a teststub package. P6 may or may not introduce one; it's not in P2's scope.

