## 7. Compile-time and test-time checks

### 7.1 `Factory` signature pin

```go
// var _ ensures Factory remains compatible with its archetypes. If a
// future driver's openDolt / openPostgres no longer matches, the build
// breaks. Keeps the interface stable.
var (
    _ storage.Factory = openDolt
    // P3 adds: _ storage.Factory = openPostgres
)
```

These live inside each driver package.

### 7.2 Capability coverage

The test from P1 §8 (`TestMustCapabilitiesAreImplemented`) iterates `storage.RegisteredBackends()`. P2's deliverable is the registry; the test was specced by P1 and lands in P1's implementation PR. P2's PR adds `RegisteredBackends()` so the test compiles; the body doesn't change.

### 7.3 Self-registration smoke test

```go
// internal/storage/doltdriver/driver_test.go
func TestRegistration(t *testing.T) {
    backends := storage.RegisteredBackends()
    found := false
    for _, b := range backends {
        if b == storage.BackendDolt { found = true; break }
    }
    if !found {
        t.Fatalf("BackendDolt not registered (got %v)", backends)
    }
}
```

A trivial sanity check that catches "init() didn't run" failures (e.g., if someone removes the file but forgets to remove the blank-import elsewhere).

### 7.4 Unknown-backend error test

```go
func TestOpen_UnknownBackend(t *testing.T) {
    _, err := storage.Open(t.Context(), "nope", storage.ConnectionConfig{})
    var unk *storage.ErrUnknownBackend
    if !errors.As(err, &unk) { t.Fatalf("want ErrUnknownBackend, got %v", err) }
    if unk.Name != "nope" { t.Errorf("Name = %q, want %q", unk.Name, "nope") }
    if len(unk.Available) == 0 { t.Errorf("Available is empty; expected at least 'dolt'") }
}
```

### 7.5 Duplicate-registration panic test

```go
func TestRegisterDriver_DuplicatePanics(t *testing.T) {
    defer func() {
        if r := recover(); r == nil { t.Fatal("expected panic on duplicate registration") }
    }()
    storage.RegisterDriver(storage.BackendDolt, func(context.Context, storage.ConnectionConfig) (storage.Storage, error) { return nil, nil })
}
```

Uses the Dolt name on purpose — by the time the test runs, `init()` has registered "dolt"; re-registering it must panic.

