## 9. Public SDK additions in `beads.go`

P2's PR adds:

```go
// Storage backend selection. Most callers should use Open or
// OpenFromConfig (Dolt-default). For Postgres or other registered
// backends, use OpenWithBackend.
type (
    BackendType      = storage.BackendType
    ConnectionConfig = storage.ConnectionConfig
)

const (
    BackendDolt     = storage.BackendDolt
    BackendPostgres = storage.BackendPostgres
)

// OpenWithBackend opens a Storage for the named backend. The driver MUST
// be registered, typically by blank-importing
// "github.com/steveyegge/beads/internal/storage/<driver>".
//
// The dolt driver is registered by importing the beads package. Other
// drivers (postgres, teststub) require an explicit blank import.
func OpenWithBackend(ctx context.Context, name BackendType, cfg ConnectionConfig) (Storage, error) {
    return storage.Open(ctx, name, cfg)
}

// RegisteredBackends returns the sorted list of registered backend names.
func RegisteredBackends() []BackendType {
    return storage.RegisteredBackends()
}

// ErrUnknownBackend is returned by OpenWithBackend when the named
// backend has not been registered.
type ErrUnknownBackend = storage.ErrUnknownBackend
```

The existing `Open(ctx, dbPath)` and `OpenFromConfig(ctx, beadsDir)` keep their signatures and behavior. They're shortcuts for the common Dolt path; rewriting them onto the registry path is a follow-up that doesn't block P2 or P3.

To make `beads.OpenWithBackend(BackendDolt, …)` work without forcing every consumer to also blank-import doltdriver, `beads.go` adds an internal blank-import:

```go
import (
    // ...
    _ "github.com/steveyegge/beads/internal/storage/doltdriver" // ensures BackendDolt is registered
)
```

This preserves the SDK's "import beads, get a Dolt store" promise. Consumers wanting Postgres add their own `_ "github.com/steveyegge/beads/internal/storage/postgres"` (lands in P3).

