## 3. Server-Side Session Manager

### 3.1 Session interface and concrete types

File: `internal/storage/rpc/iter_session.go` (handwritten)

```go
// serverIterSession is the common interface for all server-side iterator sessions.
// Each concrete type wraps a typed storage.Iter[T].
type serverIterSession interface {
    TypeName() string      // "issues", "events", etc. for error messages
    LastUsedAt() time.Time
    Touch()
    Close() error
}

// Concrete per-type session: one per Iter* method (generator emits these)
// Example for issues:
type issueIterSession struct {
    iter      storage.Iter[types.Issue]
    ctx       context.Context
    cancel    context.CancelFunc
    typeName  string        // "issues"
    lastUsed  int64         // atomic: unix nano
    mu        sync.Mutex    // serializes Next calls
}

func (s *issueIterSession) TypeName() string      { return s.typeName }
func (s *issueIterSession) LastUsedAt() time.Time { return time.Unix(0, atomic.LoadInt64(&s.lastUsed)) }
func (s *issueIterSession) Touch()                { atomic.StoreInt64(&s.lastUsed, time.Now().UnixNano()) }
func (s *issueIterSession) Close() error          { s.cancel(); return s.iter.Close() }
```

### 3.2 iterSessionManager

```go
// iterSessionManager manages all server-side iterator sessions.
type iterSessionManager struct {
    mu       sync.RWMutex
    sessions map[string]serverIterSession // sessionID → session

    maxCap     int           // daemon_iter_max, default 64
    idleReap   time.Duration // daemon_iter_idle_seconds, default 30s
    stopCh     chan struct{}
    stats      *iterStats    // shared with daemonServer stats
}

type iterStats struct {
    sessionsActive     atomic.Int64
    sessionStartsTotal atomic.Int64
    sessionReapedTotal atomic.Int64
    rowsStreamedTotal  atomic.Int64
}
```

### 3.3 openSession — cap enforcement

```go
func (m *iterSessionManager) openSession(id string, sess serverIterSession) error {
    m.mu.Lock()
    defer m.mu.Unlock()
    if len(m.sessions) >= m.maxCap {
        return storage.ErrTooManyIterators
    }
    m.sessions[id] = sess
    m.stats.sessionsActive.Add(1)
    m.stats.sessionStartsTotal.Add(1)
    return nil
}
```

`IterXxxStart` generates a UUIDv4, opens the underlying `storage.Iter`,
calls `openSession`, and returns the sessionID. On `ErrTooManyIterators`,
the server populates `reply.RPCError` with `Kind: "ErrTooManyIterators"` and
returns `nil` (per the be-oyer9z error envelope pattern).

### 3.4 Idle reaper goroutine

```go
func (m *iterSessionManager) reapLoop() {
    // Check at half the idle interval for timely reaping without busy-spin
    ticker := time.NewTicker(m.idleReap / 2)
    defer ticker.Stop()
    for {
        select {
        case <-m.stopCh:
            m.drainAll()
            return
        case <-ticker.C:
            m.reapStale()
        }
    }
}

func (m *iterSessionManager) reapStale() {
    now := time.Now()
    m.mu.Lock()
    defer m.mu.Unlock()
    for id, sess := range m.sessions {
        if now.Sub(sess.LastUsedAt()) > m.idleReap {
            sess.Close()
            delete(m.sessions, id)
            m.stats.sessionsActive.Add(-1)
            m.stats.sessionReapedTotal.Add(1)
        }
    }
}

// drainAll is called on daemon shutdown to close all open sessions cleanly.
func (m *iterSessionManager) drainAll() {
    m.mu.Lock()
    defer m.mu.Unlock()
    for id, sess := range m.sessions {
        sess.Close()
        delete(m.sessions, id)
    }
}
```

`drainAll` is triggered by the `stopCh` close, which the daemon's shutdown
path calls before exiting. This ensures backend cursors are released even
when the daemon exits cleanly (e.g., idle timeout, max lifetime expiry).

### 3.5 Session lifecycle state machine

See the Excalidraw diagram: `be-60kmhm-session-lifecycle.png`

States: OPENING → OPEN → ACTIVE (Next in progress) → IDLE → REAPED | CLOSED

```
IterXxxStart ──→ [OPENING]
                     │ openSession() succeeds
                     ↓
                   [IDLE]  ←─────────────────────────────────────────┐
                     │ IterXxxNext arrives                            │
                     ↓                                                │
                  [ACTIVE] ─── batch returned ──────────────────────→┘
                     │ Done==true OR RPCError
                     ↓
                 [EXHAUSTED] ─── auto-close ──→ [CLOSED]

            [IDLE] ─── idle > 30s ──→ reaper fires ──→ [REAPED]
            [IDLE | ACTIVE | EXHAUSTED] ─── IterClose ──→ [CLOSED]
            daemon shutdown ──→ all sessions ──→ [CLOSED]
```

